Sources of the graphs used by this repository

Graphs that are NOT redistributed here (tools/fetch_datasets.py downloads or rebuilds them and checks
their SHA-256):

  citeseer.lg, mico.lg, test1.lg, test2.lg
      Copied without change from the GraMi distribution, Datasets/ of
      https://github.com/ehab-abdelhamid/GraMi (M. Elseidy, E. Abdelhamid, S. Skiadopoulos, P. Kalnis,
      "GraMi: Frequent Subgraph and Pattern Mining in a Single Large Graph", PVLDB 7(7), 2014).
      citeseer.lg is derived from the CiteSeer dataset (LINQS). The GraMi repository is distributed under
      the GNU LGPL 2.1, whose text does not address the data files.

  email_eu.lg
      Converted from SNAP email-Eu-core-temporal and email-Eu-core department labels
      (https://snap.stanford.edu/data/email-Eu-core-temporal.html, https://snap.stanford.edu/data/email-Eu-core.html).
      The SNAP pages state no licence.

  lastfm.lg, github.lg
      Converted from SNAP MUSAE LastFM Asia and GitHub
      (https://snap.stanford.edu/data/feather-lastfm-social.html, https://snap.stanford.edu/data/github-social.html).
      The SNAP pages state no licence.

Graphs that are redistributed here:

  string_ecoli.lg
      Converted from STRING v12.0, Escherichia coli K-12 (taxon 511145), file 511145.protein.links.v12.0.txt.gz,
      keeping the interactions with a combined score of at least 500. STRING data are available under the
      Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence (https://string-db.org/cgi/access); D. Szklarczyk et al.,
      "The STRING database in 2023", Nucleic Acids Research 51(D1):D638-D646, 2023.

  bitcoin_otc.lg
      Converted from SNAP soc-sign-bitcoin-otc (https://snap.stanford.edu/data/soc-sign-bitcoin-otc.html).
      The SNAP page states no licence.

  example.lg
      The example graph of the paper, created for this repository.
